 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The damsel of the Isaurian mountains\nWould have been rapt in passion and delight\nIn our prime, if their natural charms\nHad not acted on her and our\nHusbands; she bore a man to heaven,\nAnd, like him that bears an angel down,\nWas witness to her heavenly birth\nOf some other apparition of\nFaith: he loved his wife for such reason;\nThe rest were swept away by passion\nBy mezzo-fine language, which was spoken\nTo her too strangely, as it appears",
